phase P3
title Core
description
    **Class:** not readily verifiable.

    **Kind:** verification-suite.

    **Goal:** the core's first slices on production: the consolidation, lane policies, Runtime life, write-ahead,
    restore, the compiler and actor identity. The core and its checks grow together, one area at a time.

    **Starts when:** P2's completion audit passes, so one test style is left and generated Stories exist. The
    orchestrator then opens this phase's Tasks.

    **Order:** @task.V3.T54, @task.V3.T18, @task.V3.T55, @task.V3.T19, @task.V3.T20, @task.V3.T17, @task.V3.T9, the
    order the user set; then @task.V3.T79 (code convergence with the step's edit operations), @task.V3.T86 (fixture
    layout), @task.V3.T85 (capture on issue), @task.V3.T84 (no caps), @task.V3.T87 (bench), @task.V3.T88 (tsrs),
    @task.V3.T83 (fast tests), T20's close, @task.V3.T81 (construction bugs) and @task.V3.T80 (the user, 2026-11-16;
    reordered by the user's Q14 A, 2026-11-17). A `blocked_by` link is a real dependency only; where several Tasks are
    ready, take the earliest in this order.

    **Verified by:**

    - per area, the Story tests, run rules and compile-time tests written from its Spec, in
      `packages/flow-state-v3/tests/`, run by `vp test`;
    - `nub run faults`: each new rule adds a planted fault to code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts, and the tests
      must catch it;
    - the suite's coverage record, started by @task.V3.T67 and extended by each Task here;
    - skill:check-task per Task; `nub run check` and `nub run lint:rules` at zero.

    **One iteration:** the next ready Task: its Spec change, written just in time; its requirements as failing checks,
    with a planted fault for each new rule; the core change; the bench; an independent skill:check-task. The user's page
    is written at each slice's close.

    **Exit criteria:**

    - every Task is done;
    - every Requirement these Tasks build has a check that passes and that failed on its planted fault;
    - `nub run faults` catches the dead core and every named fault at the final revision;
    - the suite's coverage record is updated, and an audit by a lead that did not build the suite has
      passed (skill:policy-testing#audit-a-suite);
    - the completion audit names each Plan outcome these Tasks satisfy and finds it delivered.

    **False pass:** a test written from the code instead of the Spec; a rule with no planted fault.

    **Caught by:** the review of each Task's first commit, which maps every requirement to a Spec rule, and `nub
    run faults`.

    **Gates:**

    - `nub run faults`, which rejects the dead core and the named faults in code:packages/flow-state-v3/tests/faults.ts;
    - `nub run lint:rules`, which rejects the planted violations in code:tools/flow-state-lint/imports.test.ts
      and code:tools/flow-state-lint/rules.test.ts;
    - `nub run check`.

    **Failure limit:** 2.

    **Stops:**

    - a guarantee that can't be met;
    - public entry-point names or a large public API change.

    **User's read:** each Spec revision; each changed expected result with its reason; small public API calls; the
    user's page at each slice's close.

    **Draws from:**

    - skill:policy-verification (prove a suite; the coverage record);
    - skill:policy-testing (the requirements as failing checks first);
    - skill:to-spec for an area's Spec change and skill:to-design per module;
    - skill:execute-task and skill:check-task per Task; skill:review at a Task's first commit and its close;
    - skill:policy-convergence at the threshold; skill:diagnose when a test fails unexplained.

    Every Task below is a draft. Before starting its lead, the orchestrator writes its full text with skill:to-task
    (requirements, approach, acceptance by Spec rule). The earlier text of each, in `wiki/tasks/V3/` at commit
    `6b9fe478`, was written for the conformance suite: it is background only, and its acceptance does not carry over.
    The old suite's known gaps for each Task are in Appendix A
    of code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/test-system-2026-11-15.md.
tasks
    T54
        title       Core consolidation: owed-endings ledger, one start, diff-written records, acts into evidenceOf
        status      done
        priority    high

        description
            Finish the core consolidation: one ledger of owed endings, one `start`, records written from what each step
            touched, and every report built by `evidenceOf` from acts.

            **Why now:** most of it is in the core at this revision; the rest was paused when the conformance suite was
            deleted, and every later core Task builds on the consolidated shape.

            **Read first:** @spec.WriteLanes (its `algorithm` section: the ledger), @spec.Actors,
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/ledger.ts, code:packages/flow-state-v3/src/core/evidence-of.ts. The
            paused step's plan is `wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/t54-a3-prep-2026-11-15.md` at commit `4f4ac9f5`.

            **Risk:** what is left is not listed here. The first step is to read the paused plan against the code and
            write the remaining requirements as failing checks. The old Task's "production self-proof" is replaced by
            the planted faults.

            May change: `src/core/`, `src/host/`, `tests/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a consolidation that moves code without changing who owns each fact → caught by a run rule per
            fact (one delivery per ending, one writer per record) and its planted fault.
        acceptance
            - The ledger, `start`, record writes and `evidenceOf` are each the one place their work is done, shown by
              Story tests and run rules that cite @spec.WriteLanes and @spec.Actors.
            - The two known bugs of this area (a flush that holds only its own actor's record; an adopted lane's later
              endings routed against Turn R20 and I26) are fixed, and their inverted tests are flipped.
            - `nub run faults` catches every named fault; `vp test` and `nub run check` pass.
