            per-walker text memo stays on and relies on Turn R24's contract. 7: the fourth red was not reproduced under
            the 8-copy load. The likeliest is generated.stress 'session-nests-deep: stress runs from fixed seeds', which
            took 49.5 s of its 60 s budget alone; owner @task.V3.T83, which also owns printing every name. Routed, not
            blocking (each probed): (a) the comparator gets three kinds wrong. A DataView's bytes are ignored. A RegExp
            in a Set or a Map key is keyed by lastIndex. Cyclic Set members give an order-dependent answer (Equal says
            equal) and a missed change (Equal says differ). Tests missed it: same.test's kinds have no DataView, RegExp
            member or cyclic member. (b) Past 64 levels, a decoding default's effect runs once per walk: 200 missing
            keys get one shared value from 66 calls, where Effect makes 200 calls. A pure default is unaffected. Tests
            missed it: the differential samples are shallow and have no defaults. Fix: key the kept outputs by position.
            (c) The freezer skips a Map, Set or Date the app froze itself, so its set, add and setTime still work in
            dev. Also unfrozen: typed arrays, #private fields and a selector's raw return. Turn R24's 'class instances
            included' overclaims. Tests missed it: immutable.test freezes only fresh containers. (d) A name the host
            cannot write says 'the input field P/Album of P/Album', which drops the reason (Codec R4). Tests missed it:
            deep-inputs asserts only not RangeError. (e) tx.ts has an orphaned Env doc whose text says production
            freezes. (a) to (e) go to @task.V3.T79. (f) inputOfName turns an undecodable restored name into {} (older;
            Codec R5), owner @task.V3.T20. (g) print.ts redactables and sweep.ts carries recurse, owner @task.V3.T83. No
            outside imports or temporary names. Sidecars (4 Haiku, one blind): accepted (a) to (g). Changed:
            ArrayBuffer, since Equal also calls two buffers equal, which matches R6. Rejected: format-1 recursion
            (above); comments on unexported code (the package's lint-bomb style, check at 0).

    T74
        title       App mix: several fixtures in one Runtime
        status      done
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@task.V3.T70]
        description
            Run several fixtures in one Runtime with generated Stories, sharing storage, the network, the clock
            and reloads.

            **Why now:** a fixture alone never meets another machine's write in the same batch, a storage refusal during
            another machine's capture, or a reload with one lane held and another queued. The app-mix profile finds bugs
            between features that no single fixture reaches (the user accepted it as its own Task after
            @task.V3.T70, 2026-11-16).

            **Read first:** the app-mix profile in
            code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/fixture-catalogue-2026-11-11.md, @plan.Testing.O6, @task.V3.T70.

            **Approach:** starts once three or more fixtures can share one Runtime; a failing run shrinks by dropping
            whole fixtures first, then steps.

            May change: `src/host/testing/`, `tests/generated/`, `fixtures/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a mix whose fixtures never touch a shared resource → caught by counting, per run, the steps that
            hit shared storage, network, clock or a reload.
        acceptance
