        description
            One convergence pass removes the structural debt the whole-codebase review found, without
            changing behaviour.

            **Why now:** the review found the step state with no edit operations (whole-world copies on every write,
            O(n²) per step, retire and interrupt blocks written two or three times), lifecycles built from flags and
            side maps, 17 small duplicates with no single home, and host code that leaves Effect; every later slice
            builds on these files.

            **Read first:** code:wiki/plans/flow/references/proposals/code-quality-review-2026-11-16.md (sections 1 to 3
            and 5 to 10, and its order in section 10), AGENTS.md "Code style (v3 production)",
            code:tools/lint-bomb/STYLE.md, code:tools/lint-bomb/FLOW-STATE.md.

            **Risk:** six behaviour questions came up (the review's section 9); two may be bugs: a local actor of a
            persisted machine declined `NoPersistence`, and an actor name whose input skips the JSON codec. Each gets a
            Story naming the wrong side before any change; one that changes public behaviour goes to the user first.

            **Approach:** the review's section 10 order, steps 1 to 5, 7 and 8; step 6, the second harness, is
            @task.V3.T80. Bench before and after step 3.

            May change: `src/`, `tests/`, `bench/`. Evidence: this Task's comments.

            False pass: a refactor that keeps the tests green because they never reached the moved code → caught by `nub
            run faults` with every fault caught by its own target, run before and after.

            User's read: any section 9 question whose answer changes public behaviour.
