              before and after numbers are reported, and where a regression stays, the comment names what each lost
              second buys and the lead asks the user.
            - Each fixture Story's count is set from the bench and recorded in the Story (fixtures.md).
            - The same Story ids, test counts and fault caught list hold before and after; the dead core still runs the
              full suite.
            - No timeout is raised without a measured reason.
            - Every test-tooling guard has one source and a measured size (the user, 2026-11-17, Q5 A): the Story turn,
              settle-task and advance limits; the faults run's timeout, copies (from CPU and memory) and output buffer;
              the stress and generated-Story test timeouts; the generator's weights, lengths and shrink budgets; Story
              advances read the capture interval instead of a literal.
            - `nub run check` and `nub run lint:rules` pass; a new speed note with the baseline is in V3.log.
