    T88
        title       Type-aware lint and type check on tsrs: vite-plus upgraded, same diagnostics, faster check
        status      open
        priority    medium
        blocked_by  [@T87]
        description
            `nub run check` runs type-aware linting and type checking on the `tsrs` backend: `vite-plus` upgraded to
            1.7.0 or later and `tsrs` added, with the same diagnostics as today and the check's time and memory recorded
            before and after.

            **Why now:** Oxlint now offers `tsrs`, a Rust port of TypeScript, as the type-aware backend in place of
            tsgolint (https://oxc.rs/blog/2026-11-17-faster-type-aware-linting-with-tsrs): the same 61 rules, and up to
            7x faster combined type checking and linting with up to 75 % less memory (vendor numbers). `vite.config.ts`
            already sets `lint: { options: { typeAware: true, typeCheck: true } }`, so Oxlint picks `tsrs` up once
            installed (the user, 2026-11-17).

            **Read first:** `vite.config.ts` (`lint`), `package.json` (`check`, `lint`, pinned `vite-plus` 1.3.0,
            `oxlint`, `typescript`), the blog post above, @task.V3.T87 (record the timing in its `tooling` concern).

            **Risk:** `vite-plus` 1.3 to 1.7 also moves `vp test` and the formatter; the custom JS lint plugins
            (lint-bomb, flow-state-lint, the vite-plus plugin) run in the same pass; `tsrs` is new and lists no known
            limitations, so a missing diagnostic would weaken a gate. The trial runs in a scratch copy first; the live
            tree changes only when nothing is lost. Exact versions are pinned.

            May change: `package.json`, the lockfile, `vite.config.ts` (only if the upgrade requires it). Evidence: this
            Task's comments.

            False pass: a backend that reports fewer problems passes a clean tree → caught by planted errors (a type
            error, a floating promise, an unsafe `any`, a lint-bomb rule breach) that must fail before and after.
        acceptance
            - Before and after, on the same machine: `nub run check` diagnostics on the clean tree (expected zero) and
              on each planted error, its wall time and peak memory (recorded with `nub run bench tooling --record` if
              T87's tool is ready, else in a comment), and the package suite's counts.
            - The planted errors fail `nub run check` both before and after, with matching diagnostics; the clean tree
              passes both.
            - `vite-plus` is pinned at 1.7.0 or later and `tsrs` is pinned exactly; `nub run check`, `nub run
              lint:rules`, the formatter and the package suite give the same results as before.
            - If anything is lost (a diagnostic, a test, a plugin), the live tree is left unchanged and the gap is
              reported instead.
        comment     2026-11-17T16:52:19Z
            Agents (the user, 2026-11-17): a Sonnet builder and a Sonnet reviewer for this Task, not the usual
            Opus review.
